      },
      "text": "Camp 1 – Mutanzi – Camp 2/3"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9b6259b0400bb5c47748f0bb3126fd41600d3b61de84feeefe81857ae9a220b0",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9la9dr-5gsd40eg",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Set out early from Camp 1 after breakfast. After about 2 hours on foot, you’ll reach the community of Mutanzi and learn about the daily life and traditions of its Indigenous residents.\n\nContinue on foot for about 40 minutes to Camp 2, where a hot lunch is included. Along the trail and near the camp, you can see the Buritaca River and the surrounding mountains.\n\nThe next stop is Camp 3, Mamo Romualdo. In the local community, a mamo is regarded as a keeper of wisdom. The walk to the camp follows the river and takes about 4 hours.\n\nOver dinner, your guide will talk about Tayrona culture and explain the plan for the next day. Accommodation may be in hammocks, beds or tents. Dinner is included.\n\nDuration: 7 hours. Distance: 14 km. Elevation: 900 m."
    },
